  "question": {
    "text": "A particle is moving in a straight line. The variation of position ' $x$ ' as a function of time ' $t$ ' is given as $x=\\left(t^3-6 t^2+20 t+15\\right) m$.\nThe velocity of the body when its acceleration becomes zero is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VC9sF",
      "text": "$6 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EaVHw",
      "text": "$10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3Ltx4",
      "text": "$8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "T5HuS",
      "text": "$4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Displacement, $x=t^3-6 t^2+20 t+15$\n$\\therefore$ Velocity, $v=\\frac{\\mathrm{dx}}{\\mathrm{dt}}=3 \\mathrm{t}^2-12 \\mathrm{t}+20$\n$\\therefore$ Acceleration, $a=\\frac{d v}{d t}=6 t-12$\nWhen $a=0$\n$\\Rightarrow 6 \\mathrm{t}-12=0 \\Rightarrow t=2 \\mathrm{~s}$\nAt $\\mathrm{t}=2 \\mathrm{~s}, v=3(2)^2-12(2)+20=8 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
    "image": null
  },
